(986, 'Plurals: Phrase Level Animals Adventure (Vol. 20)', 'Interactive interactive genially deck targeting auditory memory and syntax development through engaging animals activities designed for speech-language pathologists.', 1, 'Auditory Memory', 'Syntax Development', 'Language', 'Plurals', 'Phrase', 'Interactive Genially Deck', 'Animals', 'https://view.genially.com/embed/64a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d006?lesson=986', 'Begin with warm-up cues focusing on correct tongue position and relaxed posture. Prompt the student to imitate model productions before independent attempts. Reinforce positive efforts with immediate auditory and visual feedback.', '/thumbnails/lesson-3.jpg', 15, 'Digital interactive deck, dry-erase marker, student response tokens.', 'Student will accurately produce or demonstrate Plurals in phrase contexts with 80% accuracy across 3 sessions.', 'Review student baseline targets. Have visual cue cards accessible.', 229, 986, 1, 153, '2026-10-18 10:45:11'),
(987, 'Initial /L/: Isolation Level Seasonal Adventure (Vol. 20)', 'Interactive teaching script targeting phoneme production and expressive elaboration through engaging seasonal activities designed for speech-language pathologists.', 4, 'Phoneme Production', 'Expressive Elaboration', 'Articulation', 'Initial /L/', 'Isolation', 'Teaching Script', 'Seasonal', NULL, 'Present the target visual stimulus and ask the student to identify the target element. Provide verbal prompts: ''Remember to use your snake sound /s/'' or ''Keep your voice smooth and continuous''. Record baseline accuracy over 10 consecutive trials.', '/thumbnails/lesson-4.jpg', 20, 'Digital interactive deck, dry-erase marker, student response tokens.', 'Student will accurately produce or demonstrate Initial /L/ in isolation contexts with 80% accuracy across 3 sessions.', 'Review student baseline targets. Have visual cue cards accessible.', 574, 987, 1, 383, '2026-10-18 17:57:11'),
(988, 'Perspective Taking: Phrase Level Food & Cooking Adventure (Vol. 20)', 'Interactive assessment targeting theory of mind and visual processing through engaging food & cooking activities designed for speech-language pathologists.', NULL, 'Theory of Mind', 'Visual Processing', 'Pragmatics', 'Perspective Taking', 'Phrase', 'Assessment', 'Food & Cooking', NULL, 'Guide the student through the interactive deck step-by-step. Encourage multi-sensory awareness by having the student feel airflow or watch mouth movements in a mirror. Transition from carrier phrases to open-ended conversational retell.', '/thumbnails/lesson-5.jpg', 25, 'Digital interactive deck, dry-erase marker, student response tokens.', 'Student will accurately produce or demonstrate Perspective Taking in phrase contexts with 80% accuracy across 3 sessions.', 'Review student baseline targets. Have visual cue cards accessible.', 748, 988, 1, 499, '2026-10-19 01:09:11'),
